    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20-a5">

                <pb facs="0116" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg22"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 253.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gilbert to Mr. Jussen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Trieste</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 22,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    inclosed papers relating to the application for a passport lately made by Mrs.
                    Charles Mundé.</p>
                <p>I beg leave to differ with Mr. Lee, and would say that I think the State
                    Department would consider an indentification by one of its consuls as good as
                    that of any other person.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Gilbert.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
